From 3f782b59f83462bc5f8104dca7c76babe3acecc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:08:42 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(state): futility survives older record writers; doctor
 never says to stop the gateway

Two follow-ups to the holder-presence futility window (#3688):

- Mixed versions. A process still on an older release rewrites the shared
  deferral record with a fresh window whenever its own holder view differs
  from the stored one, which could starve futility until every process on
  the store was upgraded. Each process now keeps its own copy of the
  presence window and the longer of the two counts. No record at all (the
  recovery deletes it) restarts both.
- Doctor advice. The record's holder_pids is its last writer's view and
  leaves the writer out, so when a CLI process wrote it the list was the
  gateway and doctor said to stop "the listed process(es)". Doctor now
  lists the processes holding state.db right now, names the non-gateway
  ones to stop and says to keep the host gateway running (or that the
  gateway alone holds it and its retry rebuilds). Holder descriptions
  elide inline `-c` bootstrap code so the real arguments show.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
